# Local authoring tools — generated, and not meant to be published.
# The tagger and the notes editor are how Ben writes art-tags.json and
# rsi-notes.json. They live at their own URLs; publishing them from this repo
# would put an editing UI on the public site.
flounder-tagger.html
flounder-notes.html

# Generated. index.html is committed because it is what the host serves;
# flounder-search.html is the identical build output the test suites read,
# so it does not need to be in the repo.
flounder-search.html

# Test screenshots
_shot_*.png

# Junk
.DS_Store
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Build fingerprints. Small, but they are a local record of what YOUR machine
# built and when — they belong to the machine, not the repo. BUILD-REPORT.md is
# committed on purpose: it is the human-readable "what changed" for each build.
.build-history/

# scratch from syncing files onto this machine
_to_delete/il*
_wtest

# The old Playwright suites (tests/, run-tests.sh, _test_v*.js at the top level)
# were removed from the repo in the lore-tracker commit. None of them knew about
# the welcome tour added later, so on a first visit the overlay swallowed their
# clicks and 38 of 40 hung instead of reporting anything — broken tests that
# look like coverage. smoke.js is the ship gate, as HOW-WE-WORK says.
# They are still in git history if they are ever wanted back.
tests/
run-tests.sh
_test_*.js

# replaced by the real logo icons in icons/ and favicon.ico
icon.svg

# The art-tagging pipeline's local scratch. art-cache/ is the downloaded card
# art itself (gigabyte-scale) — the site serves art from Lorcast URLs via
# card-db.json, never from here. set-outputs/ and the run log are raw/backup
# tagger output already merged into the committed art-tags.json; regenerate
# either by re-running the tagger, never by hand-editing what's here.
art-cache/
art-tools/set-outputs/
art-tools/overnight-run.log
